  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Pavan Kumar Yadav vs State Of U.P. Thru. Drugs Inspector Food ... on 3 January, 2024 High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:337 Court No. - 27 Case :- Application U/S 482 No. - 12803 of 2023 Applicant :- Pavan Kumar Yadav Opposite Party :- State Of U.P. Thru. Drugs Inspector Food Sefety And Drugs Administ. Di Counsel for Applicant :- Shitla Prasad Tripathi Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Subhash Vidyarthi,J. 1. Heard Sri Shitla Prasad Tripathi, the learned counsel for the applicant and Sri Manish Kumar Pandey, the learned A.G.A-I, for the State. 2. The instant application under Section 482 Cr.P.C. has been filed by the applicant with a prayer to quash the entire criminal proceedings of case and [LEAKAGE_MASK] the order dated 29.09.2023 passed by the learned Additional District and Session Judge, court No. 7. Faizabad, in Compliant Case No. 12/2020, under Section 18c/27 of the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940, State of U.P. through its Drugs Inspector, Food Safety and Drugs Administration, Office District Magistrate, Sultanpur vs Pawan Kumar Yadav and another. 3. The applicant was summoned to face the trial on a compliant under Section 18c/27 of the Drugs and Cosmetics Act, 1940 by means of an order dated 02.03.2022 in complaint no. 12/2020. The applicant had filed an application under Section 482 Cr.P.C No. 9713 of 2020 challenging the validity of the summoning order and the application was disposed of by means of an order dated 22.12.2022 by observing that there was no ground to [LEAKAGE_MASK] the impugned proceedings but the Pavan Kumar Yadav vs State Of U.P. Thru. Drugs Inspector Food ... on 3 January, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/96025053/ 1 applicant was granted 15 days time to surrender and apply for bail. 4.",
